# Solana Code Standards

## Context
- Applied when writing or modifying Solana-related code
- Focuses on proper import organization and error handling
- Ensures consistent usage of Solana SDK types and traits

## Requirements

### Import Organization
- Group Solana imports by functionality
- Avoid duplicate imports of common types (Pubkey, Keypair, Signer)
- Prefer single grouped imports over multiple separate ones
- Use explicit imports for error types

Example of good import organization:
```rust
use solana_sdk::{
    account::Account,
    commitment_config::CommitmentConfig,
    instruction::{AccountMeta, Instruction, InstructionError},
    message::{v0, VersionedMessage},
    pubkey::Pubkey,
    signature::{Keypair, Signature},
    signer::{Signer, SignerError},
    system_program,
    transaction::{TransactionError, VersionedTransaction},
};
```

### Error Handling
- Use proper error types from solana_sdk
- Implement custom errors using thiserror
- Handle transaction errors with specific error variants
- Include context in error messages
- Extract custom error codes when handling program errors

Example of good error handling:
```rust
#[derive(Debug, thiserror::Error)]
pub enum SolanaError {
    #[error("Transaction failed: {0}")]
    TransactionError(String),
    #[error("Custom program error: {0}")]
    CustomProgramError(u32),
}

fn extract_custom_error(error: &Error) -> Option<u32> {
    if let Error { kind: ErrorKind::TransactionError(
        TransactionError::InstructionError(_, InstructionError::Custom(code))
    ), .. } = error {
        Some(*code)
    } else {
        None
    }
}
```

### Transaction Handling
- Use appropriate commitment levels
- Handle blockhash expiration
- Track transaction statuses
- Implement proper signature verification
- Use appropriate transaction configuration

Example:
```rust
let sig = client
    .send_and_confirm_transaction_with_spinner_and_config(
        &tx,
        CommitmentConfig::confirmed(),
        RpcSendTransactionConfig {
            skip_preflight: true,
            ..Default::default()
        },
    )
    .await?;
```

## Anti-patterns

### Import Anti-patterns
```rust
// Bad: Duplicate imports
use solana_sdk::pubkey::Pubkey;
use solana_sdk::signature::Keypair;
use {
    solana_sdk::{
        pubkey::Pubkey,  // Duplicate!
        signature::Keypair,  // Duplicate!
    }
};
```

### Error Handling Anti-patterns
```rust
// Bad: Generic error handling
fn process_transaction() -> Result<(), String> {
    // Using string errors instead of proper error types
}
```

### Transaction Anti-patterns
```rust
// Bad: Missing error context
client.send_transaction(&tx)
    .map_err(|e| anyhow::anyhow!("Failed"))?;  // Missing error context

// Good: Proper error context
client.send_transaction(&tx)
    .map_err(|e| anyhow::anyhow!("Failed to send transaction: {:?}", e))?;
``` 